WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.400
welcome to Northwind

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.266
Today we're looking at our co pilot data policy

3
00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:06.566
co Pilot accepts whatever you give it

4
00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:08.766
so it relies completely on you to know

5
00:00:08.766 --> 00:00:10.733
what company data is safe to share

6
00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:12.200
to figure that out

7
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.666
every piece of data has to pass a straightforward

8
00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:17.500
two question test before you paste it into the tool

9
00:00:18.166 --> 00:00:20.300
first is this already shared with me

10
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.800
through a north wind system

11
00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:24.066
and second does it contain information

12
00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:26.533
about a specific person's private life

13
00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:29.600
if the answer is yes to the first and no to the second

14
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.266
you can proceed otherwise you must stop

15
00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.766
the policy clearly breaks this down into four approved

16
00:00:35.766 --> 00:00:38.366
and four strictly prohibited data categories

17
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.466
you can freely use your own drafts and notes

18
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.966
shared internal reports

19
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.366
public information like published freight rates

20
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.766
and transcripts from teams

21
00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:48.366
meetings you actually attended

22
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.500
customer personal data

23
00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:53.233
driver personal records like medical info

24
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:56.200
payroll data and system credentials like passwords

25
00:00:56.466 --> 00:00:57.966
mistakes usually happen here

26
00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:00.600
just because a deadline is close and a file is handy

27
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.266
let's make that dividing line perfectly clear

28
00:01:03.266 --> 00:01:06.833
with a practical example a Q2 late deliveries report

29
00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.966
shared on teams with no personal info

30
00:01:08.966 --> 00:01:12.700
is approved but a Dallas Hub driver payroll spreadsheet

31
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.666
is prohibited having legitimate access to a file

32
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:17.900
does not equal permission to paste it

33
00:01:18.466 --> 00:01:20.866
next you will sort 10 real examples

34
00:01:20.866 --> 00:01:22.866
into approved and prohibited
